1
00:00:01,140 --> 00:00:03,560
One of these bottles is missing its cap.

2
00:00:03,990 --> 00:00:07,284
From another angle, the same bottle appears in a
different position.

3
00:00:07,843 --> 00:00:09,873
Our project, Visual Peer Inspector,

4
00:00:10,233 --> 00:00:14,224
explores how to identify an unusual item among
similar products

5
00:00:14,684 --> 00:00:17,404
and show the evidence across several
photographs.

6
00:00:17,944 --> 00:00:20,524
The intended setting is small-batch inspection.

7
00:00:21,242 --> 00:00:24,782
The system uses the other objects in the scene
as its reference.

8
00:00:25,172 --> 00:00:27,312
LocateAnything finds candidate objects,

9
00:00:27,732 --> 00:00:29,312
SAM separates their foreground,

10
00:00:29,762 --> 00:00:32,152
and DINOv2 extracts visual features.

11
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:36,272
Our pipeline compares the objects and combines
evidence across views.

12
00:00:36,922 --> 00:00:39,792
Sreekar will now show how this works in the web
app.

13
00:02:41,263 --> 00:02:45,003
Our main study used 2,000 selected ToysAD-8K
scenes:

14
00:02:45,313 --> 00:02:46,723
1,000 for development,

15
00:02:46,923 --> 00:02:50,653
600 for calibration and 400 for internal
evaluation.

16
00:02:51,133 --> 00:02:56,133
With five views, assisted top-1 accuracy was
61.72%,

17
00:02:56,513 --> 00:02:59,213
compared with 22% for Automatic.

18
00:02:59,633 --> 00:03:03,583
These are tie-aware averages across predefined
view combinations.

19
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:09,303
The assisted benchmark used dataset-supplied
object matches, rather than a human-user study.

20
00:03:09,963 --> 00:03:14,168
The routes also use different scoring rules, so
matching alone does not explain the gap.

21
00:03:15,513 --> 00:03:19,703
Automatic matching remains unreliable, and
supplementary dataset results were lower.

22
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:23,773
Historical exposure to related dataset objects
also limits the evaluation.

23
00:03:24,333 --> 00:03:27,643
We have not established false-alarm rates for
all-normal batches

24
00:03:27,643 --> 00:03:29,843
or measured operator time savings.

25
00:03:30,253 --> 00:03:33,263
The potential value is a clearer inspection
review process,

26
00:03:33,593 --> 00:03:37,086
but the current prototype cannot certify that a
batch is defect-free.

27
00:03:38,863 --> 00:03:43,083
Next, we would improve matching and
independently test normal and unusual groups.

28
00:03:43,453 --> 00:03:45,983
We delivered a working prototype with measured
limits,

29
00:03:46,484 --> 00:03:49,314
turning photographs into evidence an operator
can review.
